{"schemaVersion":1,"id":"reference:d9d49a7570c05a34","name":"M12-L Kimogila Heavy Fighter","source":{"id":"source:reference-d9d49a7570c05a34","title":"M12-L Kimogila Heavy Fighter","revision":20698,"timestamp":"2024-08-26T00:21:08Z","sha256":"63b7fea8023ffc394bb11b40b89a19059ffd937ea4139a1b4edf4f5a4d4ad9cd","url":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?oldid=20698","history":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?title=M12-L%20Kimogila%20Heavy%20Fighter&action=history"},"article":{"sourceId":"source:reference-d9d49a7570c05a34","blocks":[{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Reference Book: ",{"tag":"a","children":["Rebellion Era Campaign Guide"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Rebellion_Era_Campaign_Guide"}]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["Like the ",{"tag":"a","children":["Dunelizard Fighter"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Dunelizard_Fighter"},", the M12-L Kimogila was designed and built by MandalMotors for sale to planets, corporations, and large criminal fleets or private organizations. Officially an update of the Dunelizard, the Kimogila is actually a much heavier and more robust Starfighter that violates Imperial policy regarding military vessels sold to civilians. However, by the time of its design, the Empire no longer considers snubfighters a serious threat, and as long as MandalMotors continues to be guided by a (bribable) Imperial advisor, such transgressions are overlooked.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["The M12-L Kimogila includes four linked lasers, a missile launcher with a large magazine, and a small payload of proton torpedoes. Because either the ",{"tag":"a","children":["Vehicle Pilot"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Vehicle_Pilot","referenceId":"reference:4aff6d0e54fff36e"}," or the ",{"tag":"a","children":["Gunner"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Gunner","referenceId":"reference:0cbc0bc5729f801f"}," can control the ",{"tag":"a","children":["Proton Torpedoes"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Proton_Torpedoes","referenceId":"reference:89c41c332c03f2dd"},", the ship can fill a variety of attack roles, at least for short periods of time. As a planetary bomber, it can make attack runs with both of its missile weapons; in space conflict, it can focus on making attacks with its lasers, reserving its missiles and torpedoes for heavier targets. This versatility, coupled with its remarkable resilience, makes the Kimogila one of the most popular Rebellion Era ",{"tag":"a","children":["Starfighters"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Starfighters","referenceId":"reference:e127af2636e147fc"}," for unaligned forces that need to do more with less.\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h4","children":["Default (Normal)"]},"\n",{"tag":"h2","children":["M12-L Kimogila Heavy Fighter Statistics (CL 10)"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["Gargantuan ",{"tag":"a","children":["Starfighter"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Starfighter"},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Initiative"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Initiative","referenceId":"reference:3e687de48a6ad4e5"},":"]}," +4; ",{"tag":"b","children":["Senses:"]}," ",{"tag":"a","children":["Perception"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Perception","referenceId":"reference:bd18e320a6bb9f53"}," +5\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h3","children":["Defenses"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Reflex Defense"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Reflex_Defense"},": 17 (",{"tag":"a","children":["Flat-Footed"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Flat-Footed"},": 13), ",{"tag":"a","children":["Fortitude Defense"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Fortitude_Defense"},": 28; +8 Armor\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Hit Points"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Hit_Points","referenceId":"reference:58e8ee2c9538d027"},": 160; ",{"tag":"a","children":["Damage Reduction"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Damage_Reduction"},": 10; ",{"tag":"a","children":["Shi